c207ab79->f20a47d2) with uptime 0 confirmed, rabbitmq-server active, cluster_status shows all 3 nodes running, TLS verified\"},{\"requirement\":\"Data/cluster health and quorum preserved across full restart sequence\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-146d1405e188490a\",\"cmd-c4fd0b1befd546f7\",\"cmd-842b176c61aa4a0e\",\"cmd-4f9f56504b5d4a0e\",\"cmd-9199c7ce0ccd4141\"],\"summary\":\"Durable quorum queue created and published to before restarts; after all 3 sequential node restarts the queue still shows the message (messages:1, all 3 members online) and the original message body was successfully consumed over mTLS, proving no data loss and full cluster/quorum recovery\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed a 3-node RabbitMQ cluster (node1/node2/node3, AlmaLinux 9) using RabbitMQ 3.13.7 + Erlang 26 (installed from GitHub release RPM + EPEL, since RabbitMQ 4.x required Erlang 27 which wasn't available). Created a dedicated self-signed CA and issued per-node server certs (SAN = hostname+IP) plus a client cert, all under /tmp/ca on node1. Configured rabbitmq.conf on all nodes to disable plaintext AMQP (listeners.tcp = none), serve AMQP only via TLS on 5671 with ssl_options.verify = verify_peer and fail_if_no_peer_cert = true (mutual TLS, CA-issued client certs required). Clustered all three nodes via a shared Erlang cookie and rabbitmqctl join_cluster. Enabled the management plugin (15672) on each node and restricted it via firewalld rich rules to the 10.100.214.0/24 cluster subnet only (5671 left open, 15672/4369/25672 scoped to subnet). Verified: TLS handshake succeeds with a CA-issued client cert and is rejected (fatal alerts: certificate_required / bad certificate) with no cert or an untrusted self-signed cert, on all three nodes; a full AMQPS publish/consume round-trip works via pika with mTLS; management API is reachable from cluster peers. Completed the mandatory node-restart protocol: captured boot_id + cluster/queue health baselines, rebooted node1, node2, then node3 one at a time via `systemctl reboot` (quorum preserved throughout — a replicated quorum queue's Raft leader migrated node1→node2→node3 across the sequence), polled each node until reachable again, confirmed changed boot_id and uptime≈0 as direct restart proof, and confirmed RabbitMQ rejoined the cluster (3/3 running nodes) with TLS listeners back up after each restart. Final check: the message published to the durable quorum queue before the restart sequence was still present and was successfully consumed over mTLS after all three nodes had been rebooted.","actions_performed":["Installed erlang (EPEL) and rabbitmq-server 3.13.7 (GitHub release RPM) on node1, node2, node3","Set up /etc/hosts and cluster SSH keys on all nodes","Generated a dedicated CA and per-node TLS server certs + a client cert + an untrusted cert for negative testing on node1, distributed to node2/node3 via scp","Configured rabbitmq.conf: TLS-only AMQP listener (5671) with verify_peer + fail_if_no_peer_cert, management on 15672, classic_config cluster peer discovery, pause_minority partition handling","Shared Erlang cookie across all 3 nodes","Opened firewalld rules: 5671 open globally, 4369/25672/15672 restricted to 10.100.214.0/24 cluster subnet","Joined node2 and node3 to node1's cluster via rabbitmqctl join_cluster after fixing firewall-blocked Erlang distribution","Created admin user, deleted default guest user","Verified mTLS enforcement (accept valid CA cert, reject no-cert and untrusted-cert) via openssl s_client and RabbitMQ logs on all 3 nodes","Verified end-to-end AMQPS publish/consume with pika using CA-issued client cert","Verified management API reachable cluster-internally and firewall-restricted externally via nft ruleset inspection","Created a durable quorum queue replicated across all 3 nodes with a persistent test message","Executed mandatory node-restart protocol: captured boot_id + health baseline, restarted node1, node2, node3 sequentially via systemctl reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed boot_id change + uptime reset, confirmed RabbitMQ/cluster/TLS recovery and quorum queue leader failover after each restart","Final verification: consumed the pre-restart message over mTLS after all restarts, confirming data durability"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"RabbitMQ cluster across node1/node2/node3","command_ids":["cmd-c5cb613530fe4662","cmd-1e3bad3751074edd"],"summary":"cluster_status shows all 3 nodes (rabbit@node1/2/3) as Disk Nodes and Running Nodes"},{"requirement":"AMQP over TLS using CA created for this cluster","command_ids":["cmd-09a7036bf1634b32","cmd-070dc483037c4592","cmd-dfbb97f612794f62","cmd-eabdd46c07bf446e","cmd-935101a0aaa94d5f"],"summary":"CA generated on node1, node certs signed and verified against it, listeners.tcp=none + listeners.ssl.default=5671 configured, and a full pika AMQPS publish/consume succeeded using the CA-issued client cert"},{"requirement":"Accept only client connections presenting a CA-issued certificate","command_ids":["cmd-f48b9c82d4f94ae3","cmd-cad32dba585c4d90","cmd-ad60796f7fcf4b5f","cmd-731381db8c5b4fec","cmd-6c2d0a76d1224581","cmd-64191fc0ae8e4a8b","cmd-3a6398145e084d3a"],"summary":"Valid client cert handshake succeeds (Verify return code 0); no-cert and untrusted-cert attempts are rejected with fatal TLS alerts (certificate_required / bad certificate) confirmed via openssl s_client, server logs on node1/2/3, and a pika-level rejection"},{"requirement":"Management interface reachable only within the cluster","command_ids":["cmd-c219c4c3f6474afe","cmd-bded94e2b14b409c"],"summary":"nft ruleset shows port 15672 accept rule scoped to source 10.100.214.0/24 only (no broader allow), and management API confirmed reachable from a cluster peer (node1->node2)"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: healthy baseline","command_ids":["cmd-a69471d6f03b4835"],"summary":"Pre-restart boot_id captured plus active rabbitmq-server and full 3-node cluster_status"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: ack